@startuml P2P_Payment_HappyPath
title P2P Payment — Happy Path
autonumber

actor Client
participant "API Gateway" as GW
participant "Transaction Orchestrator" as ORCH
participant "Fraud Detection Service" as FRAUD
participant "Payment Processing Service" as PAY
participant "Account Service" as ACC
database "Redis Cluster" as REDIS
database "PostgreSQL + Citus" as DB
queue "Kafka Event Bus" as KAFKA
participant "Notification Service" as NOTIF

Client -> GW: POST /transactions (idempotency_key, amount, src, dst)
GW -> ORCH: forward request
ORCH -> REDIS: GET idempotency_key
REDIS --> ORCH: not found
ORCH -> FRAUD: evaluate(transaction)  **[sync, 15ms SLA]**
FRAUD --> ORCH: APPROVED
ORCH -> PAY: processPayment(txn)
PAY -> ACC: debit(sender, amount)
ACC -> DB: SELECT balance, version WHERE account_id = sender
DB --> ACC: balance, version = v
ACC -> DB: UPDATE accounts SET balance -= amt, version = v+1\nWHERE account_id = sender AND version = v
DB --> ACC: 1 row updated
ACC --> PAY: DEBIT_OK
PAY -> ACC: credit(receiver, amount)
ACC -> DB: UPDATE accounts SET balance += amt, version = v+1\nWHERE account_id = receiver AND version = v
DB --> ACC: 1 row updated
ACC --> PAY: CREDIT_OK
PAY -> DB: INSERT ledger_entries + outbox_event (same DB transaction)
DB --> PAY: COMMIT OK
PAY --> ORCH: SUCCESS(transaction_id)
ORCH -> REDIS: SET idempotency_key -> result (TTL 24h)
ORCH --> GW: 200 OK
GW --> Client: 200 OK (transaction_id, status = COMPLETED)

== Asynchronous fan-out (happens AFTER the client already has a response) ==
PAY ->> KAFKA: [async] outbox relay publishes txn-completed event
KAFKA ->> NOTIF: [async] consume event
NOTIF ->> Client: push notification (sub-second propagation, FR-008)
@enduml

@startuml P2P_Payment_Failure1_Duplicate
title P2P Payment — Failure Scenario 1: Duplicate Submission (Idempotency Short-Circuit)
autonumber

actor Client
participant "API Gateway" as GW
participant "Transaction Orchestrator" as ORCH
database "Redis Cluster" as REDIS

note over Client: Client's first request timed out on the network,\nso it retries with the SAME idempotency_key

Client -> GW: POST /transactions (idempotency_key=X, ...)  **[retry]**
GW -> ORCH: forward request
ORCH -> REDIS: GET idempotency_key = X
REDIS --> ORCH: FOUND — cached result (transaction_id, status=COMPLETED)
ORCH --> GW: 200 OK (same transaction_id, no reprocessing)
GW --> Client: 200 OK

note over ORCH: The original transaction was already fully processed.\nNo second debit/credit occurs — satisfies FR-002 and FR-003.
@enduml

@startuml P2P_Payment_Failure2_InsufficientBalance
title P2P Payment — Failure Scenario 2: Insufficient Balance
autonumber

actor Client
participant "API Gateway" as GW
participant "Transaction Orchestrator" as ORCH
participant "Fraud Detection Service" as FRAUD
participant "Payment Processing Service" as PAY
participant "Account Service" as ACC
database "PostgreSQL + Citus" as DB

Client -> GW: POST /transactions (amount=5000, src, dst)
GW -> ORCH: forward request
ORCH -> FRAUD: evaluate(transaction)
FRAUD --> ORCH: APPROVED
ORCH -> PAY: processPayment(txn)
PAY -> ACC: debit(sender, 5000)
ACC -> DB: SELECT available_balance WHERE account_id = sender
DB --> ACC: available_balance = 1200
ACC -> ACC: check 1200 >= 5000 ? NO
ACC --> PAY: INSUFFICIENT_BALANCE
PAY --> ORCH: FAILED(reason=INSUFFICIENT_BALANCE)
ORCH -> DB: UPDATE transactions SET status=FAILED, failure_reason=INSUFFICIENT_BALANCE
ORCH --> GW: 402 Payment Required
GW --> Client: 402 { error: "INSUFFICIENT_BALANCE" }

note over ACC: No debit was ever applied — the balance check happens\nbefore any write, so no compensation is needed here.
@enduml

@startuml P2P_Payment_Failure3_ShardFailureCompensation
title P2P Payment — Failure Scenario 3: Receiver's Shard Fails Mid-Transaction (Saga Compensation)
autonumber

actor Client
participant "API Gateway" as GW
participant "Transaction Orchestrator" as ORCH
participant "Payment Processing Service" as PAY
participant "Account Service" as ACC
database "PostgreSQL + Citus\n(Sender Shard)" as DB_S
database "PostgreSQL + Citus\n(Receiver Shard)" as DB_R

Client -> GW: POST /transactions (amount, src, dst)
GW -> ORCH: forward request
ORCH -> PAY: processPayment(txn)
PAY -> ACC: debit(sender, amount)
ACC -> DB_S: UPDATE accounts SET balance -= amt WHERE account_id = sender
DB_S --> ACC: 1 row updated
ACC --> PAY: DEBIT_OK  **<<saga step 1 committed>>**

PAY -> ACC: credit(receiver, amount)
ACC -> DB_R: UPDATE accounts SET balance += amt WHERE account_id = receiver
DB_R --> ACC: **connection timeout — shard unreachable**
ACC --> PAY: SHARD_UNAVAILABLE

PAY --> ORCH: PARTIAL_FAILURE(step=CREDIT, reason=SHARD_UNAVAILABLE)
note over ORCH: Saga detects step 2 failed AFTER step 1 already committed.\nThe compensating transaction for step 1 must now run.

ORCH -> PAY: compensate(reverse debit on sender)
PAY -> ACC: credit(sender, amount)  **<<compensating action>>**
ACC -> DB_S: UPDATE accounts SET balance += amt WHERE account_id = sender
DB_S --> ACC: 1 row updated
ACC --> PAY: COMPENSATION_OK
PAY --> ORCH: COMPENSATED

ORCH -> DB_S: UPDATE transactions SET status=REVERSED, failure_reason=SHARD_UNAVAILABLE
ORCH --> GW: 503 { error: "RECEIVER_SHARD_UNAVAILABLE", status: "REVERSED" }
GW --> Client: 503 — transaction reversed, please retry

note over Client: Sender's balance is back to its original value.\nNo money was lost or duplicated — FR-001 atomicity preserved.
@enduml
